WEBVTT

00:16:58.369 --> 00:17:02.156
it's really daunting to be a senior leader
who can't talk the lingo.

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:03.382
AG: That's Rachel Barton.

00:17:03.841 --> 00:17:05.398
Last year, she landed a new job

00:17:05.422 --> 00:17:07.805
as director of technology at a bank.

00:17:07.829 --> 00:17:09.377
But there was one problem.

00:17:09.401 --> 00:17:12.233
Rachel didn't have much
experience in technology.

00:17:12.257 --> 00:17:15.289
Her coworkers might as well
have been speaking another language.

00:17:15.313 --> 00:17:17.694
RB: I had a massive dose
of impostor syndrome.

00:17:17.718 --> 00:17:19.239
AG: Impostor syndrome,

00:17:19.263 --> 00:17:21.783
the belief that you don't
deserve your success.

00:17:21.807 --> 00:17:24.769
Surveys suggest that more
than half of people have felt it.

00:17:24.793 --> 00:17:28.361
RB: Some days, in the depths
of a hundred acronyms per meeting,

00:17:28.385 --> 00:17:29.764
it was pretty tough.

00:17:29.788 --> 00:17:34.375
CMBD, DDE, HPSM, IDR, LOB,